Makes the rendering terminal depend on an explicit `opts.pty`.

Upstream, `M.cmd` opens a terminal as soon as `ft` is absent (git previews when
`builtin` is false, preview.lua:303). Rendering then goes through a terminal that
redraws on every picker refresh, hence the flicker.

This line CANNOT be moved to configuration: `pty` is still computed as upstream
does and is still used to size and start the process, only the creation of the
rendering channel changes. Going through the options would alter the four other
uses of `pty`.

The rest of the snacks customisations (picker actions, chafa preview) lives in
lazy.lua and no longer needs a patch.

